{"aggregate_type":"task","event_type":"PlanRevised","offset":200,"payload":{"added":[],"event_type":"PlanRevised","plan_ref":"9810030e4c85066df1ed82db70d9c5e2a59d11941b76ade600fa0cae8e8a2856","reason":"Reproduction status note: verify.run shows 2/2 passing because the baseline suite has no test for \"0\" — the defect is UNREPRODUCED by the suite by construction. Direct reproduction evidence exists instead: shell.exec (output_ref 29c9840086fdf611bdd47cfcf003eb62b13bf01d8a9eee65d42178bdb49d6572) shows parse_quantity(\"0\") returned 0 with no ValueError, violating the stated invariant that quantities are strictly positive. The change is still right: the goal explicitly requires ValueError for zero; the fix generalizes the existing guard (value < 0 → value <= 0) and the new test makes the failure suite-reproducible going forward.","removed":[],"version":2},"sequence":12,"task_id":"02fb3e6778854ef939164731c620719a"}
